#: {{syn|es|chachi|bacán|chévere|chido|Thesaurus:guay}}

=====Usage notes=====
* This adjective is most often treated as invariable, with the form {{m|es||guay}} being used regardless of gender or number; however, the plural form {{m|es|guais}} is also often found. Hence, “They're very cool” may be expressed either as {{m|es||son muy guay}} or as {{m|es||son muy guais}}.

====Adverb====
{{es-adv}}

# {{lb|es|Spain|slang}} [[cool]], [[terrific]]

=====Usage notes=====
* Sometimes expanded to {{m|es|guay del Paraguay}} or {{m|es|guay de Paraguay}}.

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|es|osp|guay||woe}}, from {{der|es|la|vae||woe}} or {{der|es|got|𐍅𐌰𐌹||woe}}, the latter from {{der|es|gem-pro|*wai}}, both from {{der|es|ine-pro|*wai}}. Cognate with {{cog|pt|guai}} and {{cog|it|guai}}.

